WEBVTT

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.450
(No one knows whether Kamui is divine or evil.)

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.625
(Tonight, a violent wind sweeps through the frozen land again.)

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:30.250
(People call this, \"Kamui Mau\", the Wind of God.
As it beats against the earth,)

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.800
(people bow and tremble in fear.)

00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:22.225
Jiro!

00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:36.750
(SAI INN)

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:44.500
(THE VILLAGE OF SAI, SHIMOKITA PENINSULA)

00:02:03.925 --> 00:02:04.875
Sister Sayuri!

00:02:08.375 --> 00:02:09.100
Mother.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.325
Mother!

00:02:13.525 --> 00:02:14.675
Mother...

00:02:29.925 --> 00:02:35.525
(THE DAGGER OF KAMUI)

00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:38.075
Murderer!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.625
Someone come quick!

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.550
Jiro killed Tsuyu and Sayuri!

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.700
What a horrible child!

00:02:50.425 --> 00:02:52.700
N... No, no!

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.350
What have you done?

00:02:57.125 --> 00:02:58.675
How could you kill the ones

00:02:58.675 --> 00:03:02.275
who took you in as an abandoned baby and
raised you with love?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.625
How ungrateful! You're a demon!

00:03:07.525 --> 00:03:09.275
No, I didn't do it!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.525
Then what's with that dagger? There's blood
dripping from it!

00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:14.375
This is...

00:03:14.575 --> 00:03:16.925
You'll be crucified for killing your parent!

00:03:19.725 --> 00:03:21.875
I didn't do it!

00:03:54.200 --> 00:04:00.200
(DANGO)

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.525
Anything over there?

00:06:04.575 --> 00:06:10.525
Don't let him get away!

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.550
Boy...

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.300
Do not worry.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:02.025
I know very well that you did not kill

00:07:02.725 --> 00:07:05.475
your mother and sister.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.925
The culprit is ninja.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:20.475
By now, he is being hunted and cornered
at Hotokegaura.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.500
Accept your defeat, Taroza!

00:08:14.425 --> 00:08:16.650
You have no way to escape!

00:08:17.475 --> 00:08:20.400
Hanzo, show yourself!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:35.025
Was it you who killed my innocent wife and daughter?
Or Tenkai?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:39.450
I killed them, on orders from my master.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:43.675
Needless to say, it was nothing but a trap to
lure you here

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.125
and execute you as a traitor.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:54.050
We, the Matsumae Ninja clan, couldn't enter
this land for 12 years,

00:08:54.425 --> 00:08:56.800
since we couldn't break the barrier.

00:08:57.275 --> 00:09:00.800
You do not know that your murdered wife Tsuyu
picked up and

00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:05.525
raised an abandoned baby. It's a boy.

00:09:07.225 --> 00:09:09.950
A Japanese-Ainu boy.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.475
You see where I'm going?

00:09:12.775 --> 00:09:16.400
When you infiltrated Shinopirika-kotan
long time ago, you fell in love

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.925
with an Ainu girl. It's the child she gave birth to.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.450
See it with your own eyes!

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:27.850
He's the culprit, boy.

00:09:34.525 --> 00:09:35.725
Jiro...

00:10:35.675 --> 00:10:37.375
Jiro...

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:00.075
Do not let a single villager who knows

00:11:00.475 --> 00:11:03.000
about this incident live.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.950
Burn the village down!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:20.000
Although he was a traitor, he was lucky enough to
die in front of a temple.

00:11:21.025 --> 00:11:26.825
We all become Buddha when we die. May your soul
rest in peace.

00:11:30.275 --> 00:11:32.025
Do not worry.

00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:35.400
The crabs will take care of his body.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:43.950
(SHIRAKAMI)

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.400
I hear that you were an abandoned baby.

00:11:46.425 --> 00:11:50.125
Didn't anyone tell you anything about
your father?

00:11:54.425 --> 00:11:58.050
Your father might also be a Karin.

00:11:58.225 --> 00:12:01.775
How about it, boy? Do you wish to solve the

00:12:01.775 --> 00:12:04.425
mystery of your own birth?

00:12:41.875 --> 00:12:43.550
These two are probably the

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:46.650
keepsakes of your real mother and father.

00:12:51.075 --> 00:12:54.925
I'm sure you'll be able to verify that one day.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.925
(EZO, MATSUMAE)

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.150
(SHIRAKAMI)

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.025
Take him.
(TENGEN TEMPLE)

00:13:19.075 --> 00:13:19.700
Yes, sir!

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:29.100
Don't be disrespectful to the master!

00:13:29.525 --> 00:13:30.650
Master?

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.350
He is the high priest of the Tengen temple.
He's worshiped

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:38.125
around here as a living Buddha.
He is Bishop Tenkai.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.850
Young Lord, I brought the boy.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:42.875
Young Lord!

00:13:43.175 --> 00:13:44.575
Sanpei, I'm up here.

00:13:55.125 --> 00:13:57.100
I shall train you to become a ninja.

00:13:57.925 --> 00:14:00.300
I won't go easy on you. Understood?

00:15:29.775 --> 00:15:30.950
Well done.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.775
You've become stronger, Jiro.

00:15:47.525 --> 00:15:51.750
As I've promised you, I did some digging about
your father.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:59.950
As I thought, your father was a ninja.
His name was Taroza.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:11.450
Deep in the Ezo region, there's a river that the
Ainu people call \"Shishirimuka\".

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:14.750
At its headwaters, there's a mysterious mountain

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.300
called \"Kamui Nupuri\".

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:23.675
It's said to stand high in the untrodden region
within the fog,

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.925
and the Ainu people worship it like a God,

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.925
and fear it like a devil.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.125
It's a sacred mountain, which its existence is
a mystery.

00:16:31.375 --> 00:16:32.300
Taroza

00:16:32.675 --> 00:16:35.975
infiltrated into Shinopirika-Kotan, at the
foot of that mountain

00:16:35.975 --> 00:16:37.725
and has cut contact with his clan.

00:16:38.075 --> 00:16:40.725
Why he headed there and why he disappeared.

00:16:40.925 --> 00:16:44.525
Those are questions relevant to yourself.
Go find out.

00:16:50.275 --> 00:16:52.700
You don't need to return until you find the answer.

00:17:02.425 --> 00:17:03.600
Shingo.

00:17:03.825 --> 00:17:04.550
Here.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:10.325
The prey has been set free. Hunt him like a beast
and trick him into the trap.

00:17:10.725 --> 00:17:13.375
It's a gamble. See if Jiro will act in the same

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.825
manner as Taroza at the brink of his death.

00:17:17.325 --> 00:17:18.925
Do not fail!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.625
Understood.

00:17:20.925 --> 00:17:25.350
(TENGEN TEMPLE)

00:17:40.275 --> 00:17:41.875
Off to a long trip, huh?

00:17:42.025 --> 00:17:43.000
Sanpei.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.700
Do you know many ninja?

00:17:44.725 --> 00:17:45.400
Huh?

00:17:45.775 --> 00:17:47.325
Do you know one named Taroza?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.400
No.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.125
I wasn't expecting you, your Excellency.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:58.900
I stopped by on my way to the
Hakodate administration office for the

00:17:58.925 --> 00:18:00.850
deliberation on foreign ships.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.650
Though you say that,

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:05.375
you're actually here to rush us, are you not?

00:18:05.675 --> 00:18:09.975
The fate of the Shogunate government is at stake.
There better not be any mistakes.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:16.275
\"Gold is shaped by fire, and men is tested by words.\"

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:21.725
\"Though it's not a flower, the bird inside the
flower is beautiful.\"

00:18:24.425 --> 00:18:26.950
There's also a saying, \"If you want the flower,

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.200
first tame the nightingale.\"

00:18:32.975 --> 00:18:36.900
There's no need to worry. The arrow has been shot.

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:53.725
Mother!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:00.850
Mother! Mother, come here! Hurry!

00:19:06.425 --> 00:19:09.300
\"His name is Jiro. Please take care of him.\"

00:19:10.225 --> 00:19:13.100
Are you going to raise this child?

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:18.825
I feel that the boy was given to me in place of
my husband,

00:19:18.825 --> 00:19:21.100
who disappeared while out fishing.

00:19:22.225 --> 00:19:23.700
I'll do what I can.

00:19:43.675 --> 00:19:44.425
Hey!

00:19:44.425 --> 00:19:44.950
Jiro!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:48.750
Jiro!

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:54.225
(SAI INN)

00:20:50.575 --> 00:20:52.800
Stop! Stop it!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.525
My father is ill! Please!

00:20:55.525 --> 00:20:56.725
Stay out of this!

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:06.375
Please help him! They're gonna kill my father!

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:12.075
Who the hell are you?

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:32.350
Father! Father!

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:26.350
Everything is going according as planned.
Good job.

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:32.000
Now all we have to do is wait for the Ainu boy
to take Jiro to

00:22:32.025 --> 00:22:34.225
Shinopirika-Kotan.

00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:03.900
My name is Uraka.

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:05.950
I'm Jiro.

00:23:08.075 --> 00:23:09.225
What will you do now?

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:11.325
I'll go back to Kotan.

00:23:11.675 --> 00:23:12.625
I see.

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:44.225
Are you remembering your lost father?

00:23:44.775 --> 00:23:45.650
Yeah...

00:23:47.325 --> 00:23:48.600
You have anyone else?

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:51.100
My mother is in Kotan.

00:23:54.850 --> 00:23:55.725
What about you?

00:23:57.150 --> 00:23:57.750
I've...

00:23:57.925 --> 00:23:59.300
Orphan!

00:24:07.175 --> 00:24:08.850
These two are probably the

00:24:08.850 --> 00:24:11.875
keepsakes of your real mother and father.

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:16.150
I'm sure you'll be able to verify that one day.

00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:32.350
Jiro!

00:25:15.650 --> 00:25:18.750
This is the Dagger of Kamui!

00:25:20.775 --> 00:25:24.425
I see. So that's why

00:25:24.650 --> 00:25:27.225
you're carrying this dagger now.

00:25:28.750 --> 00:25:31.550
You called this \"the Dagger of Kamui\" just now.

00:25:32.275 --> 00:25:34.075
Is there a special meaning to it?

00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:35.650
Nobody knows

00:25:35.775 --> 00:25:39.950
when and why that dagger came to be

00:25:40.175 --> 00:25:42.425
in this village.

00:25:42.675 --> 00:25:47.325
However, it is said to be a gift from the Gods of

00:25:47.325 --> 00:25:48.850
forest, water and earth.

00:25:49.175 --> 00:25:54.075
For generations, it has been kept as the
village chief's family treasure.

00:25:55.250 --> 00:25:56.925
About 20 years ago,

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.375
it was given to the man who was to be married to,

00:25:59.475 --> 00:26:03.425
Oyaruru, the village chief's only daughter.

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:08.000
However, that man took Oyaruru,

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:10.650
their new born baby and the dagger

00:26:10.775 --> 00:26:14.625
and suddenly left Kotan.

00:26:14.900 --> 00:26:16.100
W... Was his name Taroza?

00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:17.600
I don't know.

00:26:19.275 --> 00:26:21.275
And what happened to Oyaruru?

00:26:22.575 --> 00:26:27.425
One day, she came back alone, left Kotan and

00:26:27.825 --> 00:26:30.875
started to live alone by the upper reaches
of this river.

00:27:15.550 --> 00:27:16.575
Jiro...

00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:20.575
Jiro!

00:27:23.450 --> 00:27:24.975
You're alive!

00:27:25.425 --> 00:27:28.550
Jiro. My son.

00:27:51.675 --> 00:27:53.225
Here's your change of clothes.

00:27:53.625 --> 00:27:54.425
Thank you.

00:28:08.725 --> 00:28:10.525
You look just like him.

00:28:11.600 --> 00:28:12.600
Is this father's?

00:28:17.675 --> 00:28:19.225
I'm glad I kept it.

00:28:19.575 --> 00:28:22.925
I buried what's left of his keepsakes in his grave.

00:28:23.775 --> 00:28:25.100
Has my father passed away?

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:28.400
It's never been confirmed.

00:28:28.625 --> 00:28:30.750
But most likely, he's no longer alive.

00:28:31.225 --> 00:28:34.150
I didn't even think that you're still alive.

00:28:38.575 --> 00:28:46.600
(HIS NAME IS JIRO. PLEASE TAKE CARE OF HIM.)

00:28:50.875 --> 00:28:52.800
I'll draw our enemy's attention.

00:28:52.875 --> 00:28:56.975
I will entrust yours and Jiro's life into this
Shishirimuka's hands.

00:29:01.025 --> 00:29:04.025
take the boat and leave this place. Got it?

00:29:05.950 --> 00:29:08.350
Father was a ninja, right?

00:29:08.750 --> 00:29:09.625
How did you know?

00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:11.300
A person named Tenkai...

00:29:11.300 --> 00:29:12.150
Tenkai?

00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:14.825
He's the devil who destroyed our family!

00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:20.725
Taroza was sent here to Kotan by his master,
Tenkai.

00:29:21.375 --> 00:29:22.425
That can't be!

00:29:22.650 --> 00:29:23.350
It's true.

00:29:24.075 --> 00:29:27.725
But he and I fell in love and when you were born,

00:29:28.025 --> 00:29:30.500
we escaped Kotan to get away from Tenkai.

00:29:48.700 --> 00:29:50.700
Jiro!

00:29:57.050 --> 00:30:00.225
Did Taroza solve the mystery of the treasure?

00:30:05.375 --> 00:30:08.625
It seems you don't know. Never mind then.

00:30:09.975 --> 00:30:13.450
Watch the traitor's fate closely!

00:30:32.250 --> 00:30:33.650
Taroza!

00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:05.550
I stabbed my father with my own hands...

00:31:12.825 --> 00:31:14.375
Jiro...

00:31:16.725 --> 00:31:18.900
Father!

00:31:26.725 --> 00:31:27.650
Jiro...

00:32:32.775 --> 00:32:34.950
What was father like?

00:32:35.975 --> 00:32:38.575
He was a strong, tender-hearted man.

00:32:39.850 --> 00:32:41.400
He was very kind to me.

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:44.425
We only lived together for a short time,

00:32:44.575 --> 00:32:47.375
but he gave me a lifetime of happiness.

00:32:49.700 --> 00:32:51.200
From what Tenkai said,

00:32:51.475 --> 00:32:54.800
Taroza was trying to solve the mystery of a
hidden treasure.

00:32:55.225 --> 00:32:58.875
But for us, there's no greater treasure than you.

00:32:59.975 --> 00:33:02.600
We can stay together...

00:33:03.475 --> 00:33:04.200
Mother...

00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:35.800
(JIRO)

00:33:36.975 --> 00:33:37.575
(MOTHER)

00:33:44.650 --> 00:33:48.425
Parent killer...

00:33:49.975 --> 00:33:52.950
You will be cursed...

00:33:55.525 --> 00:33:58.375
There has to be some mistake! Please help Jiro!

00:33:58.825 --> 00:34:03.325
I cannot do that! Mother killing is a very
grave sin!

00:34:03.675 --> 00:34:05.725
It is the law of Kotan!

00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:16.775
Jiro, struggle harder! Be more despaired!

00:34:17.025 --> 00:34:20.900
From the depth of despair, show me your
counterattack!

00:34:24.125 --> 00:34:25.100
Tenkai,

00:34:28.300 --> 00:34:29.950
how dare you!

00:34:40.700 --> 00:34:41.325
Uraka!

00:34:42.775 --> 00:34:44.675
Jiro, now's your chance!

00:34:47.550 --> 00:34:49.250
What happened to my mother?

00:34:49.725 --> 00:34:52.225
She's been buried in the cemetery.

00:34:52.550 --> 00:34:54.025
Please take me there.

00:35:11.475 --> 00:35:14.500
That new Menokokuwa is your mother's.

00:35:18.175 --> 00:35:19.450
What about that stone grave?

00:35:19.775 --> 00:35:22.275
I don't know. It's probably for a Japanese.

00:35:24.050 --> 00:35:25.575
Thanks for everything, Uraka.

00:35:26.050 --> 00:35:28.700
I don't want to cause you trouble, so let's part here.

00:35:29.775 --> 00:35:30.500
Jiro.

00:35:30.875 --> 00:35:34.850
Be well! We may meet again someday.

00:35:37.425 --> 00:35:39.875
Good bye, take care.

00:35:45.700 --> 00:35:47.225
From what Tenkai said,

00:35:47.575 --> 00:35:51.175
Taroza was trying to solve the mystery of a
hidden treasure.

00:35:51.775 --> 00:35:54.850
A mystery of a treasure? What's that about?

00:35:55.575 --> 00:35:59.175
I buried what's left of his keepsakes in his grave.

00:36:50.150 --> 00:36:51.575
Kamui Nupuri.

00:37:11.900 --> 00:37:14.275
(HIS NAME IS JIRO. PLEASE TAKE CARE OF HIM.)

00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:39.825
In heaven and earth, you are the only one I can
rely on.

00:37:40.775 --> 00:37:44.525
Right now, I don't know if going along with you will

00:37:44.575 --> 00:37:46.075
bring me misfortune or hope.

00:37:46.300 --> 00:37:50.450
But there's no going back now!

00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:33.100
Kamui Rhythmless!

00:38:36.825 --> 00:38:39.650
Young Lord, I've caught Jiro.

00:38:52.925 --> 00:38:54.350
Let's go!

00:38:54.575 --> 00:38:55.775
Where to?

00:38:58.250 --> 00:38:59.625
Hidaka Pass.

00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:04.000
Men that Magoroku went to call should be
there by now.

00:39:05.200 --> 00:39:06.550
Works fine for me.

00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:07.200
What?

00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:11.175
J... Jiro?

00:39:19.150 --> 00:39:21.100
Sing a little for me.

00:39:22.625 --> 00:39:24.725
What's this about a mystery treasure?

00:39:24.900 --> 00:39:27.200
N... Nobody knows the details.

00:39:27.275 --> 00:39:30.000
But, we know it's buried somewhere.

00:39:30.700 --> 00:39:32.375
So, it hasn't been found yet?

00:39:32.975 --> 00:39:34.850
Taroza may have

00:39:35.075 --> 00:39:38.550
found some kind of a clue about it.

00:39:38.550 --> 00:39:41.175
Why are you putting me through all this?

00:39:41.900 --> 00:39:44.800
By putting you in the same situation as
your father,

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:46.850
we expected you to act the same way

00:39:46.925 --> 00:39:49.525
and find a clue to the buried treasure.

00:39:50.800 --> 00:39:53.725
For that reason, you took me, a baby, from
Shishirimuka

00:39:53.925 --> 00:39:55.975
all the way to the beach at Sai?

00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:59.800
Such trouble you've gone through.

00:40:00.525 --> 00:40:05.275
You put... in the water...

00:40:08.950 --> 00:40:12.900
I did. The paralysis potion that you used.

00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:27.000
Listen. If Jiro has something with him,

00:40:27.025 --> 00:40:28.400
make sure you take it!

00:40:28.750 --> 00:40:31.525
That's the Master's order.

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:36.600
It's Jiro! Get him!

00:41:09.025 --> 00:41:09.700
Huh?

00:41:11.775 --> 00:41:13.170
Impossible!

00:41:14.300 --> 00:41:15.090
You fool!

00:41:24.650 --> 00:41:27.575
Take that as a souvenir and tell this to Tenkai!

00:41:28.125 --> 00:41:29.875
As of now, I'm a rogue ninja!

00:45:16.575 --> 00:45:20.275
You're wasting your time. You'll be destroyed
whatever you do.

00:47:17.075 --> 00:47:18.900
I guess you missed your chance to die.

00:47:20.575 --> 00:47:24.700
I don't think this world is

00:47:24.700 --> 00:47:27.675
worth coming back to,

00:47:27.925 --> 00:47:31.975
but now that you've recovered, just give up and
recuperate.

00:47:32.625 --> 00:47:39.550
Get rid of than shady blood thirst and wake up
your hunger instead.

00:48:08.100 --> 00:48:11.975
I'm Shouzan Ando. As you can see,

00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:14.400
I'm just a strange and stubborn old man.

00:48:26.750 --> 00:48:30.575
When I was playing with that toy over there,

00:48:30.775 --> 00:48:32.850
those stupid government officials

00:48:32.850 --> 00:48:34.850
kept coming telling me to stop.

00:48:35.450 --> 00:48:37.800
I got so sick and tired of them.

00:48:37.800 --> 00:48:40.675
So I left and ended up here.

00:48:45.825 --> 00:48:48.975
What I'm interested in is

00:48:49.075 --> 00:48:52.750
none of those thieves' business.

00:48:52.900 --> 00:48:53.875
Thieves?

00:48:54.550 --> 00:48:59.275
People are born naked and they become naked once
they die.

00:49:00.050 --> 00:49:02.250
All we do until we die is

00:49:02.325 --> 00:49:06.025
work, eat, shit and sleep.

00:49:06.100 --> 00:49:10.925
Whether you're a samurai, a farmer, a fishermen,
Japanese, Ainu, foreigner

00:49:10.925 --> 00:49:13.450
or any other living creatures,

00:49:13.450 --> 00:49:16.350
there isn't much difference.

00:49:17.225 --> 00:49:20.475
In short, those government officials who eat

00:49:20.475 --> 00:49:24.775
without working are thieves.

00:49:38.775 --> 00:49:42.250
I'm guessing you've been bullied by those thieves.

00:49:52.650 --> 00:49:56.950
The area that those fools govern

00:49:57.050 --> 00:49:59.625
is this place that look like a snot.

00:49:59.950 --> 00:50:05.450
This is Ezo. And this enormous area is a
foreign land.

00:50:06.275 --> 00:50:10.800
China, India, Russia, Portugal, England, America.

00:50:14.600 --> 00:50:17.600
And the sea of Ezo is now a main thoroughfare

00:50:17.600 --> 00:50:19.625
for foreign ships.

00:50:19.625 --> 00:50:23.450
Sir, a ship! There's a ship passing by!

00:50:29.400 --> 00:50:32.950
It's here! It's here!

00:50:52.575 --> 00:50:56.325
One day I'm going to sneak aboard on one of those
ships,

00:50:56.325 --> 00:51:00.775
go to a foreign land and make those
government officials kiss my ass.

00:51:15.300 --> 00:51:17.375
So? What do you think?

00:51:17.375 --> 00:51:18.525
Sir...

00:51:19.150 --> 00:51:21.325
I'm sorry. I haven't had a visitor for a while

00:51:21.325 --> 00:51:24.975
that I've completely forgotten that
you're wounded.

00:51:24.975 --> 00:51:27.600
This girl is the one who found you

00:51:27.600 --> 00:51:30.675
and helped me treat you. Her name is Chiomapp.

00:51:32.900 --> 00:51:33.700
I'm Jiro.

00:51:37.525 --> 00:51:40.300
Sir, are you familiar with foreign words?

00:51:41.225 --> 00:51:41.875
Huh?

00:51:45.600 --> 00:51:47.050
I see.

00:51:47.625 --> 00:51:50.975
For Tenkai to search so persistently for this,

00:51:50.975 --> 00:51:53.450
it must be very important.

00:51:54.150 --> 00:51:54.925
This

00:51:55.000 --> 00:51:58.375
is a duplicate I made for precaution.

00:52:00.700 --> 00:52:02.500
Please tell me what it means.

00:52:03.450 --> 00:52:04.825
Very well.

00:52:06.400 --> 00:52:09.275
Most likely, this man Tenkai is a Shogunate guardian

00:52:09.350 --> 00:52:13.775
who brought Ezo under direct control of the
Shogunate as a countermeasure

00:52:13.775 --> 00:52:16.800
against foreign ships and was later sent to Matsumae.

00:52:16.875 --> 00:52:18.100
If that's the case,

00:52:19.350 --> 00:52:21.675
you are picking a fight

00:52:21.675 --> 00:52:24.325
with the Shogunate.

00:52:25.675 --> 00:52:28.175
I'm heading over to Edo

00:52:28.200 --> 00:52:30.850
and report to his Excellency.

00:52:30.925 --> 00:52:31.525
Yes, sir!

00:52:31.850 --> 00:52:34.400
I will bring back the Matsumae Three,

00:52:34.400 --> 00:52:36.575
from Edo as well.

00:52:36.875 --> 00:52:38.925
So, where are Sanpei and Oyuki?

00:52:39.425 --> 00:52:40.775
I have left them behind.

00:53:40.325 --> 00:53:41.200
(EDO)

00:53:41.200 --> 00:53:43.100
When the man I sent to Satsuma

00:53:43.100 --> 00:53:46.050
brought back the report of the legend of the hidden gold

00:53:46.050 --> 00:53:48.400
that's been handed down for generations on

00:53:48.475 --> 00:53:51.125
Amami Island, I was rather apprehensive.

00:53:51.450 --> 00:53:54.725
But now, it seems the search was worth it.

00:53:55.125 --> 00:53:58.150
If we succeed in finding the gold, we'll be

00:53:58.750 --> 00:54:02.175
able to stop not only the foreign powers
who are demanding to

00:54:02.600 --> 00:54:05.200
open our ports, but we can also stop those clans

00:54:05.200 --> 00:54:07.100
plotting intrigue as well.

00:54:07.200 --> 00:54:11.475
And thus, we can rebuild the framework of the
Shogunate rapidly.

00:54:11.925 --> 00:54:14.600
So, what does this message say?

00:54:16.975 --> 00:54:19.675
\"Hear O Heavens and give hear O Earth

00:54:19.675 --> 00:54:21.975
for the Lord has spoken.\"

00:54:22.725 --> 00:54:26.650
\"Where the sun rises and the moon rises,
the Elysium lies.'

00:54:28.900 --> 00:54:32.100
Where the sun rises and the moon rises...

00:54:32.975 --> 00:54:34.675
What on earth does that mean?

00:54:34.700 --> 00:54:35.575
Here.

00:54:36.300 --> 00:54:37.075
Thank you.

00:54:37.625 --> 00:54:39.525
I want some, too.

00:54:47.750 --> 00:54:49.025
Here you go, sir.

00:54:49.425 --> 00:54:50.450
I got it!

00:54:51.250 --> 00:54:54.950
Th... This is it! Yes, this!

00:54:57.725 --> 00:55:00.900
Here, the sun and the moon!

00:55:01.025 --> 00:55:03.775
Jiro, remove that pieces of mother-of-pearl!

00:55:24.100 --> 00:55:25.675
There's nothing here.

00:55:44.625 --> 00:55:48.600
I... It's America! This is a map of America!

00:55:49.275 --> 00:55:52.625
Listen, you can go to America

00:55:52.850 --> 00:55:55.075
if you cross the sea like this.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:59.125
In winter, the sea is all frozen

00:55:59.125 --> 00:56:00.975
so you should be able to walk there!

00:56:02.075 --> 00:56:04.025
Anyway, if you go to Kamchatka

00:56:04.025 --> 00:56:05.700
when spring arrives,

00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:07.900
there'll be foreign ships there.

00:56:07.900 --> 00:56:10.950
If you can smuggle yourself aboard,
it should be fine.

00:56:14.475 --> 00:56:16.975
The time has come to use this.

00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:20.850
It's gold dust to pay for your passage.

00:56:21.225 --> 00:56:23.650
I'm sure you'll be able to use make good use of it.

00:56:26.825 --> 00:56:29.175
At any rate, once the mystery is solved,

00:56:29.175 --> 00:56:32.325
Jiro will be eliminated.

00:56:33.775 --> 00:56:37.975
My men who found this, called Taroza,

00:56:38.900 --> 00:56:42.725
was actually a spy sent from Satsuma clan.

00:56:42.850 --> 00:56:43.625
What?

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:49.625
He was a ninja dispatched by
Kichinosuke Saigo, a Satsuma guardian.

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:50.800
Are you saying

00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:54.625
that the Satsuma clan is involved in this matter?

00:56:56.500 --> 00:56:58.025
Do not worry.

00:56:58.375 --> 00:57:01.375
If we get to it first, there should be no problem.

00:57:06.650 --> 00:57:16.775
We, the Matsumae Three, are here.

00:57:20.950 --> 00:57:23.150
Jiro's going out to hunt.

00:57:23.600 --> 00:57:25.500
I'm healed and I must build up my body.

00:57:25.975 --> 00:57:28.200
I have no way to thank you for all you've done, so

00:57:28.400 --> 00:57:29.550
maybe I'll catch a deer.

00:57:30.525 --> 00:57:31.625
To thank me?

00:57:31.800 --> 00:57:32.200
Yeah.

00:57:33.050 --> 00:57:36.850
There's something that I want. Your shuriken.

00:57:36.850 --> 00:57:37.300
Huh?

00:57:41.975 --> 00:57:42.875
This?

00:59:15.075 --> 00:59:17.050
What's the rush?

00:59:19.625 --> 00:59:21.750
Tenkai's men have caught up with me.

00:59:22.975 --> 00:59:23.975
I must leave now.

00:59:24.025 --> 00:59:26.675
Chiomapp, where did you leave the boat?

00:59:26.750 --> 00:59:27.825
Seseki beach.

00:59:27.850 --> 00:59:28.650
Right.

00:59:29.475 --> 00:59:32.250
Listen. These are the translations from the

00:59:32.250 --> 00:59:35.175
secret message in your dagger.

00:59:35.350 --> 00:59:37.150
This is the map of America.

00:59:37.150 --> 00:59:38.400
Do not lose them!

00:59:38.550 --> 00:59:39.125
Yes.

00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:40.850
Maybe this

00:59:40.850 --> 00:59:44.575
treasure is something enormous.

00:59:46.775 --> 00:59:49.250
Hey, I told you to go back!

01:00:01.550 --> 01:00:04.850
Don't forsake your dream, make your hopes
come true.

01:00:05.225 --> 01:00:06.650
Got it, Jiro?

01:00:07.125 --> 01:00:07.700
Yes, sir.

01:00:08.300 --> 01:00:09.650
Meeting you has...

01:00:09.700 --> 01:00:10.625
Watch out!

01:00:17.125 --> 01:00:18.025
Sir!

01:00:23.875 --> 01:00:25.950
Sir, hang on!

01:00:28.875 --> 01:00:33.450
Meeting you has made me feel that my life

01:00:33.675 --> 01:00:36.925
was not worthless after all...

01:00:38.975 --> 01:00:44.375
Hey, didn't I tell you to go back?

01:00:49.625 --> 01:00:54.500
People are born naked and they become naked once
they die.

01:00:54.775 --> 01:00:57.050
All we do until we die is

01:00:57.100 --> 01:01:01.000
work, eat, shit and sleep.

01:01:01.375 --> 01:01:05.600
The area that those fools govern

01:01:05.825 --> 01:01:08.300
is this place that look like a snot.

01:01:11.000 --> 01:01:12.800
This is getting interesting.

01:01:13.575 --> 01:01:15.950
I'm feeling super excited!

01:03:36.425 --> 01:03:38.900
You have an ally?

01:03:55.950 --> 01:03:57.125
I have an ally?

01:04:02.300 --> 01:04:05.350
Jiro!

01:04:33.675 --> 01:04:37.650
You should know what Jiro and that
deceased old man

01:04:37.650 --> 01:04:40.450
discovered and talked about.

01:04:41.225 --> 01:04:46.225
If you tell me everything, then you nor Jiro
wouldn't have to die.

01:04:56.125 --> 01:04:58.150
Jiro.

01:05:04.250 --> 01:05:05.600
Fool.

01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:29.925
Wait...

01:06:20.150 --> 01:06:23.200
Thank you. Who are you?

01:06:23.975 --> 01:06:25.500
I'm Jiro.

01:06:26.775 --> 01:06:29.900
I'm Sam. Why did you save me?

01:06:29.975 --> 01:06:31.725
I want to get on a ship.

01:06:32.375 --> 01:06:34.125
A ship? My ship?

01:06:36.825 --> 01:06:38.875
I want to go to America.

01:06:44.175 --> 01:06:48.250
Okay, Jiro! You're my life saver.

01:07:12.525 --> 01:07:14.350
You're not getting away, Jiro!

01:08:22.350 --> 01:08:27.625
I see. This is for your passage, huh?
Alright, I'll take you.

01:08:29.025 --> 01:08:29.575
Huh?

01:08:30.750 --> 01:08:34.900
I'll give you one now and another one when we get
to America.

01:08:38.275 --> 01:08:39.125
Fine.

01:08:39.325 --> 01:08:43.475
But if you cause any trouble, you'll have to
get off the ship. Understood?

01:08:45.400 --> 01:08:46.550
What about her?

01:08:47.325 --> 01:08:48.350
Throw her overboard.

01:08:48.875 --> 01:08:53.675
No. I'm responsible for the lives of everyone on
this ship.

01:08:54.200 --> 01:08:56.225
You take her and look after her.

01:08:56.900 --> 01:08:57.525
No!

01:08:59.900 --> 01:09:01.000
Those are my terms.

01:09:07.575 --> 01:09:09.450
If you don't like it, get off the ship!

01:09:25.850 --> 01:09:26.850
What's wrong?

01:09:27.850 --> 01:09:28.850
She has a fever.

01:09:29.950 --> 01:09:31.925
I'll go look for a medicine.

01:10:27.175 --> 01:10:28.950
It's been two days now.

01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:33.325
She should at least drink a soup.

01:10:35.075 --> 01:10:37.050
Jiro, get some rest.

01:11:38.250 --> 01:11:41.450
Right now, our ship is here in the
Strait of Kamchatka.

01:11:42.025 --> 01:11:45.150
We'll probably stop by these ports

01:11:45.325 --> 01:11:47.475
and then down to California.

01:11:49.525 --> 01:11:50.800
Where's Los Angeles?

01:11:51.275 --> 01:11:52.650
Here.

01:11:52.950 --> 01:11:55.350
Where's Santa Catalina Island near there?

01:11:56.100 --> 01:12:01.350
Santa Catalina. Hmm, maybe this?

01:12:02.550 --> 01:12:04.100
The storm's getting stronger.

01:12:06.600 --> 01:12:09.250
You better eat before it really gets bad.

01:12:57.275 --> 01:12:58.000
What?

01:13:01.250 --> 01:13:03.925
What did you do to me while I was unconscious?

01:13:04.325 --> 01:13:05.300
Wh... What did I do?

01:13:05.650 --> 01:13:09.200
I changed your clothes, I fed you and...

01:13:11.250 --> 01:13:13.175
Why did you save me?

01:13:15.725 --> 01:13:16.525
Why...

01:13:23.200 --> 01:13:24.800
Why didn't you kill  me?

01:13:26.950 --> 01:13:29.225
Why did you save me?

01:13:42.750 --> 01:13:43.825
That's a lie!

01:13:44.400 --> 01:13:47.925
He came after my gold dust and tried to kill me!

01:13:48.775 --> 01:13:49.875
Either way,

01:13:49.875 --> 01:13:52.450
the trouble started after you boarded this ship.

01:13:52.950 --> 01:13:56.200
Now that this has happened, I have to ask you to
get off my ship.

01:13:56.700 --> 01:13:59.625
That's not fair! Jiro saved my life!

01:13:59.950 --> 01:14:02.250
If Jiro leaves, I leave too.

01:14:02.875 --> 01:14:04.200
You're a slave.

01:14:04.675 --> 01:14:06.375
You're not free to go anywhere!

01:14:08.450 --> 01:14:09.225
A slave?

01:14:09.700 --> 01:14:13.800
I bought Sam with my own money, so he's my property.

01:14:15.700 --> 01:14:18.275
Would this be enough for what you paid for him?

01:14:19.050 --> 01:14:20.525
That's not quite enough.

01:14:21.175 --> 01:14:22.625
Stop it, Jiro.

01:14:23.500 --> 01:14:24.550
This is all I have.

01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:26.850
How about it, Jiro?

01:14:27.800 --> 01:14:31.625
If you apologize to him, we can work things out.

01:14:32.350 --> 01:14:34.650
There's no reason for me to apologize.

01:14:35.525 --> 01:14:36.650
No matter what?

01:14:41.500 --> 01:14:44.600
That's a shame. I was getting to like you, but

01:14:44.600 --> 01:14:45.775
you leave me no choice.

01:14:45.825 --> 01:14:46.450
Captain.

01:14:46.750 --> 01:14:49.875
As of now, Jiro is your master. Alright?

01:14:51.875 --> 01:14:54.050
It won't be a bother if you hold on to it, right?

01:14:54.450 --> 01:14:56.225
Now, take it.

01:14:58.650 --> 01:15:00.175
As soon as we get to Kamchatka,

01:15:00.175 --> 01:15:01.925
you'll be asked to get off the ship.

01:15:02.375 --> 01:15:03.550
If you walk from there to

01:15:03.550 --> 01:15:06.950
Port Petropavlovsk, you should find
another ship.

01:15:40.000 --> 01:15:42.425
It's useless not matter how far you run.

01:15:42.500 --> 01:15:43.500
I figure.

01:15:44.525 --> 01:15:47.950
Why do you resist Lord Tenkai so much?

01:15:48.700 --> 01:15:52.225
My father, mother, foster family and the ones
who saved my life

01:15:52.950 --> 01:15:54.825
were all killed by Tenkai.

01:15:58.350 --> 01:15:59.900
What's your name?

01:16:01.450 --> 01:16:02.300
Oyuki.

01:16:05.500 --> 01:16:06.375
Your family?

01:16:06.900 --> 01:16:11.675
I was found and raised by Lord Tenkai.

01:16:22.675 --> 01:16:26.200
Do you hate me?

01:16:32.725 --> 01:16:36.075
Do you want to kill me?

01:16:45.850 --> 01:16:48.000
When Lord Tenkai catches up with us,

01:16:49.275 --> 01:16:54.150
I'll return to being just a ninja and come after
your life.

01:16:57.650 --> 01:17:00.625
Do whatever you want with me while you can.

01:17:09.875 --> 01:17:13.750
Why won't you answer me? You can do anything
you want.

01:17:13.750 --> 01:17:14.575
Stop it!

01:18:17.450 --> 01:18:18.675
Looks tasty.

01:18:19.575 --> 01:18:20.650
No...

01:18:20.925 --> 01:18:22.000
That's better.

01:18:23.925 --> 01:18:24.775
What is?

01:18:24.900 --> 01:18:26.700
I like you better that way.

01:18:30.250 --> 01:18:34.775
Master, hurry!

01:18:44.925 --> 01:18:48.925
Master, I'm glad! Now we can cross over to America.

01:19:13.325 --> 01:19:14.225
Huh?

01:19:16.100 --> 01:19:19.375
Tenkai! So he did come.

01:19:20.350 --> 01:19:24.525
Sam, I can't guarantee your safety from now on.
We part here.

01:19:26.900 --> 01:19:28.400
You get on the ship.

01:19:28.825 --> 01:19:31.675
No! If master lives, then I live.

01:19:32.050 --> 01:19:33.875
If master dies, I die too.

01:19:33.875 --> 01:19:34.425
No!

01:19:38.725 --> 01:19:39.850
This is it.

01:19:44.175 --> 01:19:45.200
Take care!

01:20:16.325 --> 01:20:18.600
Do not fail this time.

01:21:07.025 --> 01:21:08.350
Master!

01:21:19.650 --> 01:21:20.400
Retreat!

01:21:24.600 --> 01:21:25.500
Jiro!

01:21:25.500 --> 01:21:26.900
Run!

01:21:48.000 --> 01:21:50.725
Jiro!

01:21:50.900 --> 01:21:58.325
Master! Master!

01:22:13.625 --> 01:22:15.775
Let's try going to Santa Catalina Island.

01:22:17.000 --> 01:22:19.400
If Master is alive, he'll definitely go there.

01:22:19.400 --> 01:22:22.200
Jiro might still be buried here.

01:22:22.200 --> 01:22:24.225
I can't leave here!

01:22:26.300 --> 01:22:29.125
If we waste our time here and the killers
are alive,

01:22:29.175 --> 01:22:30.925
you'll be killed, Oyuki!

01:22:31.150 --> 01:22:34.775
If Jiro's not alive, then I don't care if they kill me.

01:22:34.925 --> 01:22:37.500
No! You tried to save my Master.

01:22:37.500 --> 01:22:38.725
So I'll protect you, Oyuki!

01:22:39.150 --> 01:22:40.800
I'm sure that he's still alive.

01:22:41.200 --> 01:22:44.225
Oyuki, you can't die until you see him again!

01:22:47.800 --> 01:22:51.000
Jiro!

01:23:24.350 --> 01:23:27.325
(AMERICA, STATE OF NEVADA)

01:24:53.275 --> 01:24:56.400
Water... Water...

01:26:04.425 --> 01:26:06.750
Make yourself at home.

01:26:07.600 --> 01:26:10.400
My home is your home.

01:26:21.200 --> 01:26:24.675
My daughter Chico. She's actually French.

01:26:24.775 --> 01:26:28.225
When she was a baby, a dying French woman was
holding on to her.

01:26:28.225 --> 01:26:31.525
We, who happened to pass by, took her and she's
lived with us since.

01:26:31.825 --> 01:26:35.650
In our tribe, we give life to those who give us life.

01:26:35.675 --> 01:26:39.875
You saved Chico's life. So, Chico is yours.

01:26:42.025 --> 01:26:43.875
It's the rule of our tribe.

01:26:54.675 --> 01:26:57.025
I believe that experiencing and sharing

01:26:57.425 --> 01:27:00.300
joy and happiness is the true way of life.

01:27:01.875 --> 01:27:05.150
Just once, I want to laugh from the bottom of
my heart.

01:27:05.200 --> 01:27:07.500
That's how I feel.

01:27:11.350 --> 01:27:12.575
Brave man.

01:27:24.625 --> 01:27:27.175
Jiro, what are you thinking?

01:27:27.450 --> 01:27:30.075
I was wondering where Santa Catalina is.

01:27:30.275 --> 01:27:31.425
I know where it is.

01:27:31.775 --> 01:27:33.450
What? Where?

01:27:34.050 --> 01:27:37.775
Beyond two mountains from here, there's a bar with
that name.

01:27:38.325 --> 01:27:39.325
A bar?

01:27:40.425 --> 01:27:42.875
What I'm looking for is an island.

01:27:44.950 --> 01:27:49.175
But maybe the person who named the bar might know.

01:28:18.650 --> 01:28:20.500
Hey, give me a drink!

01:28:29.525 --> 01:28:30.375
Excuse me...

01:28:31.425 --> 01:28:33.375
Go take another bath!

01:28:38.475 --> 01:28:40.550
I have a question about the name of this bar.

01:28:44.600 --> 01:28:47.675
Does anyone know an island called
Santa Catalina?

01:28:48.125 --> 01:28:50.275
Santa Catalina, he says.

01:28:51.900 --> 01:28:54.900
Leave. This place is only for white people.

01:28:54.950 --> 01:28:58.200
Not for dirty scums like you.

01:29:03.425 --> 01:29:05.825
Could you tell me who named this...

01:29:05.825 --> 01:29:07.350
I said get lost!

01:29:21.250 --> 01:29:25.275
Hold it! Step outside!

01:30:59.000 --> 01:31:00.075
They're both dead!

01:31:26.150 --> 01:31:28.225
My name is Mark Twain.

01:31:29.000 --> 01:31:31.850
I'm a correspondent for the Sacramento Union.

01:31:32.375 --> 01:31:35.525
You want to know about Santa Catalina Island,
correct?

01:31:35.850 --> 01:31:36.625
Huh?

01:31:38.725 --> 01:31:40.425
Are you an Indian, too?

01:31:40.800 --> 01:31:42.525
No. I'm Japanese.

01:31:42.625 --> 01:31:43.775
Japanese?

01:31:44.425 --> 01:31:48.025
Oh! The place that Marco Polo called the
\"Golden Country\".

01:31:48.025 --> 01:31:49.475
That Zipangu!

01:31:50.675 --> 01:31:52.300
Speaking of gold,

01:31:52.300 --> 01:31:55.575
that Santa Catalina Island also has a legend
of gold.

01:31:55.800 --> 01:31:57.925
It's a pretty interesting one.

01:31:59.175 --> 01:32:01.175
Europe in the 17th century was

01:32:01.175 --> 01:32:04.400
a time when people from the overcrowded land
set out to sea.

01:32:05.100 --> 01:32:07.225
European countries fought for the

01:32:07.325 --> 01:32:10.500
command of the sea. With its ongoing
disturbances of war,

01:32:10.650 --> 01:32:13.650
this era was called \"the Golden Age of Pirates\".

01:32:14.825 --> 01:32:17.400
On May 23rd, 1701,

01:32:18.225 --> 01:32:22.250
the king of pirates, Captain Kidd was executed

01:32:22.500 --> 01:32:24.975
by the River Thames. Soon after that,

01:32:25.300 --> 01:32:27.075
a strange rumor began to spread.

01:32:28.175 --> 01:32:29.150
It's said that

01:32:29.275 --> 01:32:33.225
Captain Kidd had buried a great hoard of
treasure somewhere and

01:32:33.325 --> 01:32:37.350
left a few sets of coded messages and maps for
his descendants.

01:32:37.650 --> 01:32:42.100
But they were supposedly lost before they
reached any of them.

01:32:42.750 --> 01:32:46.450
One of the places that's rumored to be where this
treasure is buried

01:32:46.450 --> 01:32:48.575
is that Santa Catalina Island.

01:32:49.075 --> 01:32:51.800
The treasure is worth ï¿¡25,000,000.

01:32:52.875 --> 01:32:55.350
In dollars, it's $100,000,000.

01:32:55.525 --> 01:32:57.700
So even if it's a hoax, it's a great story.

01:33:00.225 --> 01:33:02.500
So, which way is Santa Catalina Island?

01:33:02.800 --> 01:33:05.125
It's about 600 km south of here,

01:33:05.125 --> 01:33:06.775
in Los Angeles harbor.

01:33:16.050 --> 01:33:17.425
Thank you, Mr. Twain.

01:33:17.750 --> 01:33:20.000
But, why did you tell me all this?

01:33:21.075 --> 01:33:24.750
When I saw you, I felt my blood stirring for
some reason.

01:33:25.400 --> 01:33:26.850
After seeing you fight,

01:33:26.925 --> 01:33:29.225
I think I might know why.

01:33:29.750 --> 01:33:34.200
Since the Industrial Revolution, awareness
of time and space has completely changed.

01:33:34.500 --> 01:33:36.625
Guns and wheels have recolored the West.

01:33:36.800 --> 01:33:39.000
As more useful tools become available,

01:33:39.000 --> 01:33:43.775
people lose sight of their essential spirit and

01:33:44.175 --> 01:33:47.675
perhaps change into another kind of creature.

01:33:48.725 --> 01:33:52.550
But you have something vital that people should
never lose.

01:33:53.225 --> 01:33:57.350
I was drawn to you, who could awaken that
something in others.

01:34:06.425 --> 01:34:08.550
I have been keeping this for you,

01:34:10.925 --> 01:34:15.350
but this is something your mother had when she
passed away.

01:34:37.550 --> 01:34:40.300
(LOS ANGELES HARBOR)

01:35:12.900 --> 01:35:16.075
(SANTA CATALINA ISLAND)

01:35:31.975 --> 01:35:34.750
Stand with your back to the peak and look at
the cliff.

01:35:35.400 --> 01:35:38.325
There stands a great figure of a Saint.

01:35:41.525 --> 01:35:46.150
From where the Saint stands, find a crescent moon
in front.

01:35:48.175 --> 01:35:52.175
If you ask the light, then the shadow will answer.

01:35:55.475 --> 01:36:00.250
Immediately recognize the cross marked on
the rock

01:36:00.900 --> 01:36:03.000
and make your way inside.

01:37:08.925 --> 01:37:11.150
If you ask the light, then the shadow will answer.

01:37:12.150 --> 01:37:16.100
Immediately recognize the cross marked on
the rock

01:37:16.600 --> 01:37:18.725
and make your way inside.

01:37:30.425 --> 01:37:34.450
At the end of the passage, what you seek will
be there.

01:37:59.250 --> 01:38:02.225
Nevertheless, do not stop seeking.

01:38:02.950 --> 01:38:05.875
Know that the true light is beyond the darkness.

01:38:07.225 --> 01:38:10.900
Take it and shine the darkness of the empty world.

01:38:58.250 --> 01:39:00.275
Captain Kidd's treasure.

01:39:01.300 --> 01:39:03.000
Is this all there is to it?

01:39:11.525 --> 01:39:13.800
After all, it's only a pirate's treasure.

01:39:14.175 --> 01:39:17.625
It's not worth fighting until death for.

01:39:19.175 --> 01:39:22.500
Oh, well. Jiro, bring them to me.

01:39:23.450 --> 01:39:25.375
If you want it, come and get it!

01:39:26.025 --> 01:39:27.075
You fool!

01:39:29.400 --> 01:39:32.900
If you want to save Sanpei, who has saved your
life twice,

01:39:32.950 --> 01:39:34.500
do as I say!

01:39:35.375 --> 01:39:36.950
You didn't notice?

01:39:37.275 --> 01:39:39.600
The first time was at the foot of Akandake.

01:39:40.600 --> 01:39:42.500
Sanpei interfered and

01:39:43.125 --> 01:39:45.025
let you escape.

01:39:46.825 --> 01:39:49.725
The second time was at the Shiretoko beach.

01:39:57.850 --> 01:40:01.925
Sanpei is the one who threw the shuriken at you
to bring you

01:40:02.375 --> 01:40:05.175
back to consciousness after you fell

01:40:05.375 --> 01:40:07.275
victim to Kiheiji's spell.

01:40:09.050 --> 01:40:12.250
He deceived me by acting like a useless fool,

01:40:12.500 --> 01:40:14.800
but I saw through that long ago!

01:40:19.150 --> 01:40:20.975
He's the same as Taroza.

01:40:20.975 --> 01:40:23.950
A ninja from Satsuma who infiltrated my clan.

01:40:25.450 --> 01:40:26.475
Sanpei!

01:40:34.525 --> 01:40:39.000
Oyuki, if you kill Jiro, I will spare your life.

01:40:43.075 --> 01:40:45.625
You don't have the nerve to kill your own brother?

01:40:45.750 --> 01:40:46.850
What do you mean?

01:40:46.850 --> 01:40:51.050
Oyuki is the daughter of Taroza and Tsuyu of the village of Sai.

01:40:51.375 --> 01:40:53.625
To keep Taroza under our control,

01:40:53.650 --> 01:40:56.800
we switched Oyuki with an abandoned baby
named Sayuri.

01:40:57.000 --> 01:41:01.475
Though your mothers are different, Oyuki and you
are a real sister and brother.

01:41:03.050 --> 01:41:05.750
Indeed, blood is thicker than water.

01:41:06.475 --> 01:41:09.450
Without knowing that, you were attracted to
each other

01:41:09.450 --> 01:41:12.275
making our pursuit successful.

01:41:13.150 --> 01:41:17.500
But now, there's no reason for me to let you
both live!

01:41:25.825 --> 01:41:30.550
It's a pity to let you die a virgin.

01:41:30.550 --> 01:41:31.450
Stop it!

01:42:00.350 --> 01:42:01.475
Oyuki!

01:42:12.325 --> 01:42:14.175
Hold it, Hanzo!

01:43:03.150 --> 01:43:04.950
Jiro...

01:43:24.250 --> 01:43:26.125
Master!

01:43:28.525 --> 01:43:29.450
Oyuki!

01:43:30.975 --> 01:43:33.125
Oyuki!

01:43:36.075 --> 01:43:41.475
(OYUKI)

01:44:04.000 --> 01:44:07.175
(OYUKI)

01:44:16.125 --> 01:44:17.175
Chico?

01:44:21.475 --> 01:44:24.625
My real name is Julie Rochelle.

01:44:24.650 --> 01:44:26.450
(OYUKI)

01:44:30.300 --> 01:44:33.125
It's the same. Why do you have this?

01:44:33.500 --> 01:44:36.525
Is there a place called Nagasaki in Japan?

01:44:36.825 --> 01:44:37.400
Yes.

01:44:38.650 --> 01:44:42.025
This is my mother, Maria Rochelle's diary.

01:44:42.550 --> 01:44:46.150
According to this, my father, FranÃ§ois Rochelle

01:44:46.350 --> 01:44:49.225
was a secret agent working for the
French government.

01:44:49.500 --> 01:44:53.725
He went to Nagasaki with my mother and I was born
in Nagasaki.

01:44:54.000 --> 01:44:57.525
So, your parents were looking for this place too?

01:44:57.800 --> 01:45:01.350
Yes. But my father was killed in Nagasaki.

01:45:01.775 --> 01:45:02.550
By whom?

01:45:02.800 --> 01:45:04.325
By a ninja called Tenkai.

01:45:04.575 --> 01:45:05.400
What?

01:45:05.825 --> 01:45:07.675
But it was a draw.

01:45:08.150 --> 01:45:10.775
Apparently, my father also shot and killed Tenkai.

01:45:11.000 --> 01:45:12.100
That's impossible!

01:45:12.425 --> 01:45:13.250
It's the shadows!

01:45:14.850 --> 01:45:16.675
The one who died in Nagasaki

01:45:16.850 --> 01:45:19.500
and the one that died here were both doubles.

01:45:23.575 --> 01:45:26.150
He is capable of that.

01:45:26.950 --> 01:45:29.700
So that means, the real Tenkai is still alive?

01:45:29.725 --> 01:45:31.400
Let's return to Japan and find out.

01:45:31.975 --> 01:45:34.675
Sam's hard work got us a steamboat.

01:45:36.400 --> 01:45:38.400
Jiro!

01:45:38.550 --> 01:45:40.475
That's your boat's captain.

01:45:41.525 --> 01:45:42.625
Jiro!

01:45:44.450 --> 01:45:45.850
Captain Drasnic!

01:45:49.075 --> 01:45:52.125
So, this is the treasure of Captain Kidd?

01:45:52.850 --> 01:45:54.900
What are you going to do, Sanpei?

01:45:54.900 --> 01:45:57.825
I'm going back to Satsuma and meet with Mr. Saigo.

01:45:58.375 --> 01:45:59.125
Mr. Saigo?

01:45:59.625 --> 01:46:03.050
He's your father's and my boss. You should meet him.

01:46:03.200 --> 01:46:04.900
It would make him very happy.

01:46:05.175 --> 01:46:06.050
Why?

01:46:06.200 --> 01:46:10.050
Jiro, do you have any idea what you've
accomplished?

01:46:11.100 --> 01:46:13.250
Why do you think your father

01:46:13.325 --> 01:46:16.300
risked his life to search for this treasure?

01:46:16.500 --> 01:46:17.850
Why do you think

01:46:18.000 --> 01:46:21.425
Captain Kidd left all this treasure?

01:46:22.800 --> 01:46:24.750
If you ask the light, the shadow will answer.

01:46:25.250 --> 01:46:28.025
Immediately recognize the cross marked on
the rock

01:46:28.325 --> 01:46:29.725
and make your way inside.

01:46:30.325 --> 01:46:33.825
At the end of the passage, what you seek will
be there.

01:46:34.300 --> 01:46:36.200
Nevertheless, do not stop seeking.

01:46:36.575 --> 01:46:39.325
Know that the true light is beyond the darkness.

01:46:39.775 --> 01:46:42.950
Take it and shine the darkness of the empty world.

01:46:52.550 --> 01:46:56.950
You've challenged the Shogunate all alone

01:46:57.000 --> 01:46:58.800
and won a victory by yourself.

01:46:59.225 --> 01:47:02.025
The Tokugawa Shogunate that lasted for
300 years

01:47:02.050 --> 01:47:05.925
is crashing down with a rumble right now.

01:47:14.650 --> 01:47:20.500
(In 1868 'Keio Year 4', the Satsuma and Choshu clan
joined forces to overthrow the Shogunate.)

01:47:20.500 --> 01:47:26.800
(In January, the \"Boshin War\" broke out with
the battle of Toba and Fushimi.)

01:47:36.920 --> 01:47:39.725
There's only
(ANTI-SHOGUNATE FORCES BEGAN TO ADVANCE TO EDO)

01:47:40.050 --> 01:47:43.300
one reason why the Satsuma and Choshu clans
decided to rise

01:47:44.125 --> 01:47:48.850
and attack against the Shogunate by force.
The military funds that came

01:47:49.575 --> 01:47:51.175
from the hidden treasure.

01:47:51.175 --> 01:47:53.700
But according to the report from my men,

01:47:53.700 --> 01:47:56.275
all that's discovered were a few Spanish coins.

01:47:56.275 --> 01:47:59.725
You do not need to be concerned Lord Sadonokami.

01:48:03.850 --> 01:48:08.525
The negotiations with the French ambassador
has been concluded and the price is settled.

01:48:09.850 --> 01:48:14.825
Excellent work, Shogunate Treasurer,
Lord Kozukenosuke Oguri. So, how much?

01:48:14.850 --> 01:48:17.250
As Ezo as a collateral, $6,000,000.

01:48:17.825 --> 01:48:19.800
Then, when the Shogunate becomes secure?

01:48:19.800 --> 01:48:22.300
Ezo will become a French territory.

01:48:22.500 --> 01:48:27.000
Even if the rebel forces invade Edo,

01:48:27.325 --> 01:48:31.800
our strength is concentrated in the navy at Ezo
to commence a counterattack.

01:48:32.325 --> 01:48:35.625
Either way, the land of Ezo is to be sacrificed.

01:48:43.300 --> 01:48:44.525
He's gone.

01:48:46.500 --> 01:48:48.150
Tenkai really was alive.

01:48:48.675 --> 01:48:50.800
But I won't let you have your way with Ezo!

01:49:14.600 --> 01:49:15.675
My name is Jiro.

01:49:16.000 --> 01:49:19.000
I'm Genjuuro Fujibayashi. What brings you here?

01:49:19.425 --> 01:49:20.600
I'd like to hire ninja.

01:49:20.775 --> 01:49:23.225
Too bad. Now's not the best time.

01:49:23.450 --> 01:49:25.250
Iga, Kouga, Nabari, Negoro,

01:49:25.250 --> 01:49:28.700
all the useful ones have just been taken away

01:49:28.700 --> 01:49:31.250
by the Shogunate Guardian, Lord Tenkai.

01:49:31.425 --> 01:49:33.075
I see there's some veterans left.

01:49:34.050 --> 01:49:37.350
Only a misanthrope like me or a bunch of
weird outcasts.

01:49:37.475 --> 01:49:38.200
I don't mind.

01:49:38.725 --> 01:49:43.150
You said Sanpei sent you here. Are you someone
from Satsuma?

01:49:43.475 --> 01:49:44.025
No.

01:49:44.350 --> 01:49:46.550
Then, are you with the Shogunate?

01:49:47.250 --> 01:49:50.050
No. I'm a rogue ninja. I'm on my own.

01:49:50.475 --> 01:49:52.750
Then, why are you trying to hire ninja?

01:49:53.125 --> 01:49:56.675
I want to defeat Tenkai and avenge those who died
because of him,

01:49:56.750 --> 01:49:58.825
starting with my deceased father, Taroza.

01:50:00.200 --> 01:50:02.700
Are you Taroza's son?

01:50:03.025 --> 01:50:03.650
Yes.

01:50:04.725 --> 01:50:07.200
If you want to defeat the Shogunate's Guardian,

01:50:07.375 --> 01:50:10.825
why don't you just join the Imperial army
like Sanpei?

01:50:11.200 --> 01:50:13.475
It's not a matter of which army, because it's

01:50:13.775 --> 01:50:15.525
just a contest between soldiers.

01:50:15.925 --> 01:50:20.025
In the end, all that's going to happen is a change
of leadership.

01:50:25.350 --> 01:50:29.200
I have no cause or reason. This is my
personal battle.

01:50:29.500 --> 01:50:31.000
Interesting.

01:50:31.500 --> 01:50:34.550
He is the head of the Iga Hattori clan.

01:50:35.300 --> 01:50:39.950
Eight ninja at 5,000 ryo each. Total of 80,000 ryo.

01:50:39.950 --> 01:50:41.850
Can you prepare that amount?

01:50:42.475 --> 01:50:44.950
If it's 5,000 each, wouldn't that be 40,000 ryo?

01:50:45.725 --> 01:50:49.500
80,000 ryo. That's the number to fight against
Tenkai.

01:50:53.425 --> 01:50:55.250
You said your name is Jiro?

01:50:56.950 --> 01:51:00.025
I will accept your request.

01:51:00.225 --> 01:51:01.450
I am grateful!

01:51:13.875 --> 01:51:15.125
Tenkai.

01:51:15.600 --> 01:51:20.450
Having him as my disciple is the only regret
I have in my entire life.

01:51:20.800 --> 01:51:23.300
How long is this war gonna last?
(OSAKA)

01:51:23.475 --> 01:51:25.425
Our life is a mess because of it.

01:51:25.450 --> 01:51:26.950
Shogunate army are resisting

01:51:27.275 --> 01:51:29.375
and the navy's warships are heading to Ezo.

01:51:29.900 --> 01:51:31.825
They're planning to fight til the end.

01:51:31.975 --> 01:51:33.500
Are we in danger?

01:51:34.100 --> 01:51:35.775
It's the end for Tokugawa as well.

01:51:35.775 --> 01:51:38.600
You know the Shogunate Treasurer,
Kozukenosuke Oguri?

01:51:38.925 --> 01:51:42.775
I heard that he was beheaded by the Imperial army
at a riverbed.

01:51:57.250 --> 01:52:01.650
So, His Excellency has died. You better be alive,
Tenkai!

01:52:08.450 --> 01:52:09.525
It's loaded.

01:52:09.700 --> 01:52:11.825
Alright. I'm going.

01:52:12.000 --> 01:52:12.900
Okay.

01:52:15.975 --> 01:52:17.125
Let's go!

01:52:17.150 --> 01:52:18.700
Go!

01:52:26.575 --> 01:52:32.250
(OSAKA NARA)

01:52:40.175 --> 01:52:41.400
Have you noticed?

01:52:42.075 --> 01:52:44.125
We are indeed being followed.

01:52:52.475 --> 01:52:54.325
(NARA IGA)

01:53:16.875 --> 01:53:21.100
I have received the preparation fee of 80,000 ryo.

01:53:21.100 --> 01:53:21.700
Then...

01:53:27.900 --> 01:53:30.125
Jiro, you fell right into our trap!

01:53:30.125 --> 01:53:30.700
What?

01:53:31.000 --> 01:53:35.075
The eight Iga ninja that left here with you
have all been killed.

01:53:35.075 --> 01:53:35.775
Look.

01:53:43.375 --> 01:53:44.950
What is all this?

01:53:45.050 --> 01:53:50.625
You don't get it? They're all my men, switched along
the way.

01:53:54.625 --> 01:53:58.700
Hanzo, I kept my promise with you!

01:53:58.750 --> 01:53:59.975
Chief, you tricked me!

01:54:00.000 --> 01:54:02.700
No, and now I'll fulfill my promise with you too!

01:54:02.700 --> 01:54:03.350
What?

01:54:03.550 --> 01:54:07.725
You paid a preparation fee for 16 men. As ordered,

01:54:07.725 --> 01:54:10.650
here are the remaining eight Iga ninja.

01:55:20.475 --> 01:55:22.675
Chief, I'm sorry.

01:55:23.650 --> 01:55:27.450
Do not worry. Taroza was my son.

01:55:28.775 --> 01:55:32.075
I'm glad I got to help my grandson.

01:55:51.600 --> 01:55:52.800
Tomi of Shindo!

01:55:52.850 --> 01:55:53.975
Kokezaru of Akabe!

01:55:53.975 --> 01:55:55.150
Likewise, Nokizaru!

01:55:55.150 --> 01:55:55.925
Gon of Nomura!

01:55:55.925 --> 01:55:56.675
Likewise, Den!

01:55:56.675 --> 01:55:57.600
Matawari of Kobe!

01:55:57.600 --> 01:55:58.725
Kanpachi of Otowa!

01:55:58.725 --> 01:56:00.075
Jibachi of Tateoka!

01:56:01.000 --> 01:56:01.975
Where to?

01:56:03.150 --> 01:56:03.850
To Ezo.

01:56:18.500 --> 01:56:27.525
(On October 25th that year, the Shogunate army occupied
the Goryokaku castle in Hakodate.Ezo declared itself an independent nation)

01:56:52.050 --> 01:56:53.150
Damn it!

01:57:28.600 --> 01:57:30.175
Can you hear me, Tenkai?

01:57:30.775 --> 01:57:33.050
Jiro, so it is you!

01:57:33.700 --> 01:57:37.100
Tengen temple, Shirakami Mansion, and all will
turn into ashes.

01:57:38.000 --> 01:57:41.100
Hanzo is dead and the Matsumae clan is destroyed!

01:57:41.100 --> 01:57:43.925
Why don't you come out and we'll put an end to this!

01:57:48.075 --> 01:57:50.700
When the spring comes and the Goryokaku falls,

01:57:51.200 --> 01:57:53.675
no one will be there by your side.

01:57:54.075 --> 01:57:55.475
That's when we'll meet!

01:58:09.175 --> 01:58:09.675
Sam.

01:58:09.775 --> 01:58:10.800
Yes, Master?

01:58:10.900 --> 01:58:12.000
Don't call me Master.

01:58:12.275 --> 01:58:13.625
Yes, Master.

01:58:13.725 --> 01:58:15.525
Take care of Julie for me.

01:58:21.500 --> 01:58:22.275
Captain.

01:58:22.325 --> 01:58:22.850
Huh?

01:58:23.225 --> 01:58:27.350
You once told me that the lives of the people
on board are your responsibility.

01:58:27.900 --> 01:58:29.150
Does that still hold?

01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:31.300
Of course.

01:58:31.850 --> 01:58:33.000
That's a relief.

01:58:33.550 --> 01:58:35.575
This area will soon be a battlefield.

01:58:35.875 --> 01:58:37.675
Please take the ship somewhere safe.

01:58:37.750 --> 01:58:39.225
Okay. Understood.

01:58:40.575 --> 01:58:41.950
Genjuuro, Nokizaru.

01:58:42.675 --> 01:58:43.225
Yes.

01:58:43.650 --> 01:58:46.850
Of all the men who came with me from Iga,
only you two have survived.

01:58:52.125 --> 01:58:53.625
Thank you for everything.

01:58:54.000 --> 01:58:55.375
Jiro, you...

01:59:40.650 --> 01:59:43.000
(THE VILLAGE OF SAI, SHIMOKITA PENINSULA)

02:01:41.800 --> 02:01:47.708
(In the next spring, Battle of Hakodate broke out.
The Imperial army attacked Goryokaku.

02:08:29.050 --> 02:08:35.375
(On May 18th, 1869 (Meiji Year 2), Goryokaku fell
The Hakodate army surrendered.)

02:08:35.375 --> 02:08:42.500
(The Boshin War that lasted for one year and
five months came to an end.)

02:08:42.800 --> 02:08:44.100
Jiro!

02:08:48.800 --> 02:08:51.125
I'm glad to see you alive!

02:08:51.200 --> 02:08:53.425
So, you're Jiro.

02:08:53.725 --> 02:08:55.875
This is Mr. Saigo.

02:08:57.800 --> 02:09:02.175
Sanpei has told me about you. I finally got to
meet you.

02:09:05.575 --> 02:09:09.125
Do I remind you of someone?

02:09:37.825 --> 02:09:42.325
(THAT YEAR, EZO WAS RENAMED HOKKAIDO.)
